abstract: >-
  QSOL UFF v5.3.0 retains the v5.2.0 reproducible astrophysics,
  falsification, provenance, witness, replay-gate, ensemble-boundary,
  telemetry, and Lean 4 assurance systems while adding a reusable nonclaim
  calibration vocabulary and a machine-readable worked reference. The release
  explicitly separates existence, robustness, genericity, prevalence,
  empirical support, and physical truth, and records forbidden epistemic
  promotions such as can-form to likely-to-form and theoretical possibility to
  empirical occurrence. The worked reference is Jampolski and Rezzolla,
  Formation of gravastars, arXiv:2509.15302v2. It is a calibration source, not
  evidence that astrophysical gravastars are generic, common, observed, or
  physically preferred.
